  "result": "Excellent! All 116 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've added per-line VAT calculation to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/invoices.js`**:\n   - Imported `roundCents` from money.js for proper rounding\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n     - Calculate VAT per line on the amount after discount: `discountedAmount \u00d7 (vatRate / 100)`\n     - Round each line's VAT individually using `roundCents()`\n     - Sum all line VATs to get invoice VAT\n     - Return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n2. **`src/render.js`**:\n   - Added VAT line display above the total\n   - Only shows VAT line when `vat > 0` (handles VAT-exempt items gracefully)\n\n3. **Tests** (24 new tests):\n   - Updated existing tests to account for VAT in totals\n   - Added VAT-specific tests covering:\n     - Single line VAT calculation\n     - VAT calculation after discount\n     - Multiple VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n     - Per-line VAT rounding\n     - VAT rendering in invoices\n     - VAT-exempt items (0% rate)\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- VAT is computed per line on the discounted amount (not the original amount)\n- Each line's VAT is rounded individually\n- Invoice VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- Total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat` (VAT is added back to get final price)\n- VAT line only displays when VAT > 0\n- Works correctly with existing discount and tier discount functionality",
